From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 12:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformBm: prune USB-NIC network boot options

EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption() creates a PXE option for every network
interface it can boot from - including the BMC's USB CDC network gadget, the
Redfish host interface (DSP0270, see RpiRedfishPkg). That is a management
link, not a boot path: it has no boot server behind it, and with the 0100
sticky-media patch an attempt would sit through a full DHCP/PXE timeout
instead of failing fast. Netboot on this board belongs to the RP1 GEM
onboard RJ45.

Prune the auto-created options whose device path carries both a MAC node
and a USB node, after the refresh in PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole. USB
mass storage has no MAC node and is untouched, as is anything an OS
installer or operator wrote. Same approach as nuc-bios-build's 0021 patch,
reduced to the USB-NIC half (this platform has no NII/SNP duplicate
problem).

Applies on top of 0004 (same file).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform specific]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
@@ -793,6 +793,69 @@
 }
 
 /**
+  Drop the auto-created network boot options for USB NICs.
+
+  EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption() creates a PXE option for every
+  network interface it can boot from. The only USB NIC on this board is the
+  BMC's CDC network gadget - the Redfish host interface (DSP0270, see
+  RpiRedfishPkg), a management link that must never be selected as a boot
+  target: netboot belongs to the RP1 GEM onboard RJ45. Recognised by a USB
+  node alongside the MAC node in the device path, which keeps this free of
+  any dependency on the Redfish package. USB mass storage has no MAC node
+  and is untouched, as is anything an OS installer or operator wrote.
+**/
+STATIC
+VOID
+PruneUsbNicBootOptions (
+  VOID
+  )
+{
+  EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION  *Options;
+  EFI_DEVICE_PATH_PROTOCOL      *Node;
+  UINTN                         OptionCount;
+  UINTN                         Index;
+  BOOLEAN                       HasMac;
+  BOOLEAN                       OverUsb;
+
+  Options = EfiBootManagerGetLoadOptions (&OptionCount, LoadOptionTypeBoot);
+  if (Options == NULL) {
+    return;
+  }
+
+  for (Index = 0; Index < OptionCount; Index++) {
+    if (Options[Index].FilePath == NULL) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    HasMac  = FALSE;
+    OverUsb = FALSE;
+    for (Node = Options[Index].FilePath; !IsDevicePathEnd (Node); Node = NextDevicePathNode (Node)) {
+      if (DevicePathType (Node) != MESSAGING_DEVICE_PATH) {
+        continue;
+      }
+
+      if (DevicePathSubType (Node) == MSG_USB_DP) {
+        OverUsb = TRUE;
+      } else if (DevicePathSubType (Node) == MSG_MAC_ADDR_DP) {
+        HasMac = TRUE;
+      }
+    }
+
+    if (HasMac && OverUsb) {
+      DEBUG ((
+        DEBUG_INFO,
+        "%a: dropping Boot%04x (USB host interface)\n",
+        __func__,
+        Options[Index].OptionNumber
+        ));
+      EfiBootManagerDeleteLoadOptionVariable (Options[Index].OptionNumber, LoadOptionTypeBoot);
+    }
+  }
+
+  EfiBootManagerFreeLoadOptions (Options, OptionCount);
+}
+
+/**
   Do the platform specific action after the console is ready
   Possible things that can be done in PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole:
   > Console post action:
@@ -922,6 +985,8 @@
   EfiBootManagerConnectAll ();
   EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption ();
 
+  PruneUsbNicBootOptions ();
+
   //
   // Record the updated number of boot configured boot options
   //
